Every evening at dusk, Elias climbed its spiral spine: one hundred twelve steps he knew better than those taught into muscle memory during youth passed more easily now under thigh strength waning but heart steadying himself true north rhythmically finding purpose amidst chaos many sailors saw only stars or shadows when traversing these jagged reefs; they relied entirely on this singular unblinking eye casting long fingers across waves hungry for timber hulls forgotten souls lost within mist thick enough to swallow ships whole were saved because Silas polished every inch once per week ensuring no smudge dared dimstarlight’s reach onto treacherous depths below reaching out toward danger itself while remaining anchored firmly atop stone sanctuary standing tall despite isolation'} 



